retention_analysis:
{% for detail in retained_details %}
<Subject {{ loop.index }}>: attribute_transfer — {{ appearance }} from <Picture {{ loop.index }}>, source person's motion, expressions, pose{% if detail %}, visibility and {{ detail }}{% else %} and visibility{% endif %}.{% if eyewear and eyewear[loop.index0] %} <Subject {{ loop.index }}> wears the eyewear from <Picture {{ loop.index }}>{% elif eyewear %} <Subject {{ loop.index }}> appears without eyewear, as in <Picture {{ loop.index }}>{% endif %}{% if eyewear %}.{% endif %}{% if hair_subject == loop.index %} Match the complete hairstyle from <Picture {{ loop.index }}>, including the hair behind the ears and at the nape.{% elif hair_outline == loop.index %} Give <Subject {{ loop.index }}> the hair outline of <Picture {{ loop.index }}> and leave the ears and neck exposed as in the portrait.{% endif %}{{ "\n" -}}
{% endfor %}
<Video 1>: partially_preserved — retain all content outside the assigned appearance edits.{% if portrait_appearance_only %} Reference pictures supply only the assigned appearance. Keep the source background and framing throughout.{% endif %}{% if occluder %} {% if occluder_exit == "lowers" %}The {{ occluder }} lowers out of frame before the next pointing gesture in <Video 1>.{% elif occluder_exit %}The {{ occluder }} passes in front of the performers and leaves the frame when it does in <Video 1>.{% else %}Keep the {{ occluder }} in front of the replacement wherever it covers the edited area in <Video 1>.{% endif %}{% endif %}{% for person in preserved_people %} Keep the {{ person }} in their own appearance and visibility from <Video 1>.{% endfor %}{% if guides %} Timeline guides establish the opening pose and composition.{% endif +%}

